 ### Concurrent 3-Stage Pipeline
 A pipeline architecture that maximizes hardware utilization by running three stages (Image Preparation, TripoSR Inference, Voxelization) simultaneously using queues and separate process pools [S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart by orchestrating CPU and GPU workloads across different processes to prevent idle time [S2, unofficial]. Choose this when dealing with heterogeneous workloads involving both CPU-intensive (voxelization) and GPU-intensive (inference) tasks [S2, unofficial]. On an M4 Pro with 48 GB RAM, processing takes ~5 seconds per emoji, with ~225 emojis completed in ~19 minutes. GPU utilization is ~80%, CPU ~60%, RAM ~23 GB [S2, unofficial]. The GPU is the bottleneck because TripoSR inference is sequential, whereas CPU stages can be parallelized and overlapped with GPU work to prevent idle time [S2, unofficial].
+
+### Separate Communication Stream with 1F1B Pipelining
+A pipelined execution strategy using two CUDA streams (computation and communication) to interleave parameter loading and gradient offloading, analogous to 1F1B (1 Forward, 1 Backward) pipelining [S3]. It sets itself apart by prefetching parameters for the upcoming microbatch while postponing gradient offloading from the prior one, using double buffering with precise timing to prevent coexistence of previous gradients and upcoming parameters [S3]. Choose this when training highly sparse scenes to maximize throughput and control memory usage [S3]. Implementation adds CUDA events to synchronize operations across streams, sets communication stream priority higher than computation stream priority, and accumulates gradients within CUDA registers before storing the sum back in CPU memory [S3].
+
+### Asynchronous Online Placement
+A technique to hide online assignment overhead by computing placement for future batches on the CPU while GPUs process the current batch [S4, unofficial]. It sets itself apart by approximating the access pattern for future batches using data collected by a profiler from previous epochs, relying on the fact that points evolve gradually during training [S4, unofficial]. Choose this when online assignment latency becomes a bottleneck during large-scale reconstruction training [S4, unofficial].
 
